We use the same SSH command to login to the next level
    root@ubuntu:~$ ssh bandit1@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
This time we are logging in with the user bandit1
we are using the password from the previous level.
6y2kwnwK6grgvwvpvLaa2T1cpFEKOhNR

The next password is stored in a file named - in the home directory
    bandit1@bandit:~$ ls
    -
    bandit1@bandit:~$ cat -
    ^C
Simply using cat - will not work as it is a file that starts with a dash.
We have to use the full path name
    bandit1@bandit:~$ cat ./-
    PK8fYLZg2hnHSz83plBL1iEPKdD3QToB

Once we add ./ before the dash we can read the password.

Password = PK8fYLZg2hnHSz83plBL1iEPKdD3QToB
